  "details": "I have created a repro scene highlighting these issues, which are only verifiable with multiple clients as everything works fine locally.\n\n1. When VRC_Trigger tries to disable a Collider with SetComponentActive on the same GameObject it is on  when the VRC_Trigger itself is not on the Root then the Collider will only disable locally and not for the network. This can be seen on the repro scene by right-clicking to check for Collider presence.\n\n2. When a VRC_Trigger tries to SetGameObjectActive the GameObject it is attached to it will disable the Root object, I believe, instead which can be see in the repro. Triggering it should only disable the GameObject with the VRC_Trigger and consequently the child GameObject which is a Sphere. However it will disable the root. This issue DOES NOT happen if the VRC_Trigger is on the root object. It won't have trouble disabling GameObjects other than the root when that is the case.\n\nThe world id for the repro: wrld_80e9e402-f8f4-4bc7-bd90-30f61a382000",
